#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "a7f1c431-54b4-52b5-9ad6-cb4dd81e0f30" :question/math-academy-id "e-151" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1.0$ | $-0.7$ | $-0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1.5$ | $2.1$ |\n\nApproximate  at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+1)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-0.3)-(-0.7)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.4}{1} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091956 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "8717eda6-57e6-59ec-ab1c-f40887fa52fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-152" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown below. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n![](images/30/3084d6ae67f37517f3d8ad0a9a62be05fe1906fcc2a24f69bd29a1e00dfd0373.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\frac{g(x+h) - g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4.$  Applying the above formula with $x=4$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+2)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091957 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "580533af-c13d-5e1c-8282-f0172709c7e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-153" :question/problem "The position of a race car along a straight track, measured in feet from the starting line, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $7$ | $12$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s'(t)$ at the time $t=0.1$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ns'(t) \\approx \\frac{s(t+h) - s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=0.1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(0.1) & ≈\\frac{s(0.1+0.1)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(0.2)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-3}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.1} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=0.1$ the velocity is approximately $40\\, \\textrm{ft}/\\textrm{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091958 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "73818e0b-6f95-59a6-b1a7-672bbea8de86" :question/math-academy-id "e-154" :question/problem "An oil tank has leaked $q(t)$ liters of oil after $t$ hours. The graph of $q(t)$ is shown below. Approximate the rate at which the oil is leaking from the tank when $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n![](images/b6/b6c5286dae7e739a588173bad9c721ae34d07f86e455e44ec9f229628cf54211.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\nq'(t) \\approx \\frac{q(t+h) - q(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=1$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{q(1+1)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $1$ hour, the tank is leaking oil at a rate of approximately $1\\,\\textrm{liter}/ \\textrm{hour}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4913166d-db60-5508-aed8-54ee253af5c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4913166d-db60-5508-aed8-54ee253af5c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315538} :answer-field/id #uuid "42c7bcbc-cf71-5b99-91e6-f63aed6760d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ad24a5a-c3d4-5218-8b93-0b9b0b21bc08" :question/math-academy-id "q-341994" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.4$ | $1.1$ | $3.7$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.6) & ≈\\frac{g(0.6+0.3)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0.9)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.1-(-0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.3} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5c46b87-58aa-5f0d-ae59-364975dfea29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5c46b87-58aa-5f0d-ae59-364975dfea29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316148} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4080e2-ea4c-5cca-98d9-ab66b5d0ff36" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2776278-e397-5818-9d00-bb84155b42d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342003" :question/problem "A function $d(y)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $d(y)$ | $-8.92$ | $-11.34$ | $-15.23$ | $-17.56$ | $-18.21$ | $-18.50$ |\n\nApproximate ${d}^{′}(y)$ at the point $y=-5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${d}^{′}(-5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{d}^{′}(y)≈\\frac{d(y+h)-d(y)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $y=-5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(-5) & ≈\\frac{d(-5+2)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{d(-3)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11.34-(-8.92)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.42}{2} \\\\  & =-1.21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5d5bdd3-94a9-59bf-b6c4-be49d93c2772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5d5bdd3-94a9-59bf-b6c4-be49d93c2772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316391} :answer-field/id #uuid "b78a1356-a5af-5e99-a19b-ab124b5e015e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22176dc8-13fa-5e60-9e3c-ce6a132e5f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342075" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d84ba0a07821011be4cf5958af44ea73e97493c5a796a0324b068fe2adca8a12.png)\n\nA car is using petrol as it travels. The graph of the amount of petrol $P(d)$, in liters, remaining in the fuel tank after traveling a distance of $d$ miles is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the amount of petrol at $d=150$ using a forward difference with step size $h=50.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the amount of petrol decreases.\n\nAfter traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is {{field-1}} liters per mile." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(d)≈\\frac{P(d+h)-P(d)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the distance $d=150$ with step size $h=50.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(150) & ≈\\frac{P(150+50)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(200)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-30}{50} \\\\  & =-0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is $-0.4$ liters per mile."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a74b16b-a1ba-514f-a14d-26c0c04983e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a74b16b-a1ba-514f-a14d-26c0c04983e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315362} :answer-field/id #uuid "d44aeb71-27ee-5525-8a16-85847bd3372c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc754b10-9417-5d37-9ac6-29d601a462cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-342079" :question/problem "![](images/84/846fc347c71ada4c01a5a85aabd0722203b84edbafcbe462064ae31d1cf2adbb.png)\n\nA drone is descending toward the ground. The graph of its height $H(t)$, in meters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the height at $t=9$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the height decreases.\n\nAfter $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is {{field-1}} meters per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{H}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{H(t+h)-H(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=9$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{′}(9) & ≈\\frac{H(9+2)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(11)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-80}{2} \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is $-40$ meters per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf22b8f6-09b5-5129-9541-3b8d03840a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf22b8f6-09b5-5129-9541-3b8d03840a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316196} :answer-field/id #uuid "da42b32b-84df-5fb0-a246-7c6e69f97114" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "870839f6-6361-5527-8457-2d1a8f03542c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342080" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae57faa04abd053e4a58d751cc084d58e07e84e0520c99a33a122f58dfd8f18c.png)\n\nA slice of jackfruit is placed in an air dryer. The graph of the moisture content $M(t)$, in percent, after $t$ hours is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the moisture content at $t=3$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the content decreases.\n\nAfter $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is {{field-1}} percent per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{M(3+2)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(5)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-40}{2} \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is $-10$ percent per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccfcdc80-0e85-5397-a64c-49cf0b75d92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3000$ people per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090497} {:answer/id #uuid "fa42f679-49a4-5656-956c-e4650d6c6b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2000$ people per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090498} {:answer/id #uuid "02701e27-5e74-5504-a903-6f81b125d1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5000$ people per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090499} {:answer/id #uuid "15c50d99-9dc9-5ea7-afc7-b6975733ac8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6000$ people per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090500} {:answer/id #uuid "2d0cbb94-4b01-5e65-b4a7-a889809f1917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4000$ people per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090501}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c03b3019-0b46-5c64-af01-3073f3e48f21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090496}] :question/id #uuid "96520ca3-f98e-5eb7-82a1-1aa5774145a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-47379" :question/problem "The population of a city is given by the function $n(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in years, from when records first began. The values of $n(t)$, in thousands, for different values of $t$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n(t)$ | $851$ | $856$ | $861$ | $865$ | $870$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of growth in population in the second year $(t = 2)$ using a forward difference approximation.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092388 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13cc7f8a-6ea7-5664-b228-b75e01609825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.6\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327103} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea62de2-8715-5939-bbf5-087f0036219e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327892} {:answer/id #uuid "730c4591-252c-5dcd-a9d7-ba4ba7057370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.2\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327930} {:answer/id #uuid "81535140-48a3-58d5-bb22-2e3e81649763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.6\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328049} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bafa3a-cd82-583f-a41e-2c11d39d5a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.8\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9bafa3a-cd82-583f-a41e-2c11d39d5a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.8\\,\\text{liters/mile}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329126} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9517da3-5ca5-5935-9c06-686c85407828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95a18afa-f8fa-5bdd-82d9-85c9a941305b" :question/math-academy-id "q-47380" :question/problem "The function $g(s)$ describes the amount of fuel, in liters, remaining in Samuel's car after driving $s$ miles. The values of $g(s)$ for different values of $s$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $s$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(s)$ | $15$ | $13.5$ | $12.1$ | $9.4$ | $8.2$ | $6.6$ | $4.8$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change in the fuel volume when $s=8$ miles using a forward difference approximation." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(s)≈\\frac{g(s+h)-f(s)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $s=8.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{g(8+2)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.6-8.2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.6}{2} \\\\  & =-0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $s=8$ the rate at which the fuel is changing is approximately $-0.8\\,\\text{liters/mile}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed37a3a-177c-5e47-a911-27f0dba20418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090515} {:answer/id #uuid "29da3137-34e7-5e6e-b088-24e7c28015b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090516} {:answer/id #uuid "379b7d29-27f8-5a7d-bf54-4ea4bf80ed26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090517} {:answer/id #uuid "44b5d065-a6a4-58f9-a7c9-1fbff8c36219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090518} {:answer/id #uuid "5f396e94-6e3a-5ec4-ac24-e35bd0dff362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090519}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c53fb680-a1c1-5a8b-be8a-fb21d5096470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090514}] :question/id #uuid "f0abb86c-6c26-5523-a3a8-a9c4c1e1ae48" :question/math-academy-id "q-47385" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f43c53ce3804de0ec59ca135a97f11e50f1022c129d87f4ea0df7bce4665d130.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y = g(x)$ is shown above.\nApproximate $g^{′}(x)$ at the point $x = 2$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h = 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092387 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a77a697-b339-5d96-98ce-1098b921ccfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327446} {:answer/id #uuid "626f616f-43cf-52ae-a77a-c298e6da8051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327794} {:answer/id #uuid "90f4c180-6dad-519a-bca5-db8695733651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328198} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ab1a1-7cf8-5dad-84b0-58b979c37ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328437} {:answer/id #uuid "ba319e6e-a347-5af3-ac80-c7b7f91e2f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3ab1a1-7cf8-5dad-84b0-58b979c37ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328437} :answer-field/id #uuid "067e48ce-1116-50af-a658-609b8280dace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43f6e718-cd5b-5458-8873-d603f1c6abcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-47388" :question/problem "![](images/15/1534153e6a5d79400a038849b48583d2ec9a62db1fc1f52a491b751e46861f51.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.$ Applying the above formula with $x=0$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0) & ≈\\frac{g(0+2)-g(0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2)-g(0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092386 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db2a2c05-4fc1-5b07-8524-1e5c2d56ee47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091673} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee0ed44-8439-52fb-8cbd-aff250e3d290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091674} {:answer/id #uuid "384641ba-762f-5d21-a28e-551e7dbde5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091675} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb796b2-7a9f-57ec-828d-6e37178f6662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091676} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec255b0-f630-5bd5-9b6f-66bf1c5792cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091677}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2fd6cbff-f267-5510-9ebc-2c717264ac2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091672}] :question/id #uuid "923940f3-d99f-59e8-8aa1-3dcaca05cfa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-9430" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $11$ | $10.5$ | $6$ | $1.4$ | $-1$ | $-2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f^{′}(x)$ at the point $x =-4$ using a forward difference approximation.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
